    <div class="header-eyebrow">Broker Opinion of Value &middot; Comparative Market Analysis</div>
    <div class="header-address">440–444 Central Ave</div>
    <div class="header-sub">Jersey City, NJ 07304 &middot; Central Avenue Corridor, The Heights</div>
    <div class="header-summary">
      <p>440–444 Central Ave is a <strong>7,473 SF</strong> assemblage improved with a two-story office/commercial building and an on-site parking lot, positioned on the Central Avenue corridor &mdash; Jersey City Heights' primary commercial spine. The site carries <strong>NC (Neighborhood Commercial)</strong> zoning and is buildable as-of-right to <strong>5 stories</strong>, with the existing improvements providing interim holding income through entitlement and design.</p>
      <p>The value conclusion is anchored to a direct, SF-based comparison against <strong>361 Central Ave</strong>, an inline 4,366 SF lot that traded for <strong>$2.6M</strong> entitled for a 22,000 GSF building with 14 units over retail &mdash; a basis of <strong>$118.18 per buildable SF</strong>, <strong>$185,714 per door</strong>, and an implied <strong>5.04x FAR</strong>. Applying that same buildable ratio to the subject's 7,473 SF lot produces an as-of-right building of roughly <strong>37,660 GSF / 24 units</strong>.</p>
    </div>
