  <div class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Value Drivers</div>
    <div class="h2">Site Highlights</div>
    <div class="highlights">
      <div class="hl-card">
        <div class="hl-head">Direct Zoning &amp; Site Match</div>
        <div class="hl-body">361 Central Ave sits in the same NC (Neighborhood Commercial) zone and shares the subject's inline, non-corner condition &mdash; making it an unusually clean, apples-to-apples comp rather than one requiring adjustment for zoning or site configuration.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hl-card">
        <div class="hl-head">Interim Holding Income</div>
        <div class="hl-body">The existing 2-story office/commercial building and on-site parking lot generate carrying income through the entitlement and design period, softening the effective basis versus a vacant comp site.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hl-card">
        <div class="hl-head">As-of-Right Density</div>
        <div class="hl-body">NC zoning permits 5 stories as-of-right, mirroring the comp's implied 5.04x FAR without the timeline or execution risk of a variance or rezoning application.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="hl-card">
        <div class="hl-head">Real-Builder Demand</div>
        <div class="hl-body">361 Central Ave was listed at $2.25M, put under contract and flipped by a local developer to an actual builder underwriting high-end condos &mdash; not a speculative flip &mdash; evidencing genuine execution demand at these bases.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

